mplex in Deoghar is a rare confluence where a sacred Shiva Jyotirlinga and a Shakti Peeth (Hridaya Peeth) reside in adjacent sanctums. The main 72-foot stone spire features a Panchasula (five-pronged trident) and is the destination for millions during the legendary 105-km barefoot Kanwar pilgrimage.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Ancient main stone sanctum housing the sacred Kamana Linga\",\n      \"Cluster of 21 auxiliary temples dedicated to diverse Vedic deities\",\n      \"Rare Panchasula trident crowning the stone shikhar\",\n      \"Epic spiritual energy during the sacred month of Shravana\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Deoghar International Airport (DGH) (8 km from temple)\",\n      byTrain: \"Jasidih Junction (JSME) (8 km) - major mainline railway hub\",\n      byRoad: \"Direct NH routes connect Deoghar with Patna, Ranchi, Kolkata, and Bhagalpur\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Keep valuables secure in cloakrooms; use official digital e-pass queues during high festival periods.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Avoid unauthorized middlemen outside temple gates; follow official temple trust queues exclusively.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"Unlike other Shiva temples which have a Trishula (3 prongs), Baidyanath temple has a rare Panchasula (5 prongs) atop its spire.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"jonha-falls\",\n    name: \"Jonha Falls (Gautamdhara)\",\n    tagline: \"Hanging valley cascade where Lord Buddha rested\",\n    type: \"famous\",\n    category: \"Waterfall & Serenity\",\n    district: \"Ranchi\",\n    location: \"Jonha, 40 km East of Ranchi\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.3444,\n      lng: 85.6072\n    },\n    elevation: \"290 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"October to February\",\n    timings: \"06:00 AM - 05:00 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"₹10 per person\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1432405972618-c60b0225b8f9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1432405972618-c60b0225b8f9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1432405972618-c60b0225b8f9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507525428034-b723cf961d3e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Also called Gautamdhara, Jonha Falls is a classic hanging valley waterfall created where the Raru River drops 43 meters to join the main plateau basin. A tranquil Buddhist shrine sits above the 722 stone steps, commemorating the belief that Gautama Buddha bathed here during his journeys across Magadha.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"43-meter hanging valley waterfall surrounded by forested knolls\",\n      \"Historical Buddhist Ashram and shrine on the upper cliff\",\n      \"Spectacular rock pools and broad stepping stones\",\n      \"Picturesque weekly tribal haat (market) on Tuesdays and Saturdays\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Birsa Munda Airport Ranchi (42 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Jonha Railway Station (1.5 km) or Ranchi Junction (40 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"40 km drive via Ranchi-Purulia highway with scenic forest stretches\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Take breaks when climbing back up the 722 stone stairs; keep hydration handy.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Do not climb onto the slippery rock ledges directly beside the upper fall crest.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"Jonha is an example of an edge knickpoint waterfall created by geological rejuvenation of the Chotanagpur river system.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"dassam-falls\",\n    name: \"Dassam Falls\",\n    tagline: \"Ten torrential streams plummeting into Kanchi gorge\",\n    type: \"famous\",\n    category: \"Waterfall & Nature\",\n    district: \"Ranchi\",\n    location: \"Taimara village, 34 km from Ranchi\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.1436,\n      lng: 85.4667\n    },\n    elevation: \"310 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"October to March\",\n    timings: \"08:00 AM - 05:00 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"₹15 per person\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1546548970-71785318a17b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1546548970-71785318a17b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1546548970-71785318a17b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1432405972618-c60b0225b8f9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Originally known as 'Da-song' in the local Mundari tribal dialect ('Da' meaning water, 'Song' meaning pouring out), Dassam Falls drops 44 meters over sheer granite cliffs. The Kanchi River splits into ten distinct sparkling streams before roaring into a deep forested canyon.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"44-meter natural cascade splitting into ten distinct streams\",\n      \"Glass skywalk & newly built cantilevered viewing bridges\",\n      \"Dramatic acoustic echo through the canyon amphitheatre\",\n      \"Surrounding virgin Sal and Mahua woodland trails\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Ranchi Airport (35 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Ranchi Junction (34 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Smooth drive along Ranchi-Tata Highway (NH-33) turning right at Taimara\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Stay behind the designated stainless steel safety railing and glass viewpoints at all times.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Swimming or bathing in the plunge pool is strictly prohibited; the underwater current has hidden cavernous under-tows.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"The name Dassam is a corruption of the Mundari phrase 'Da-Song' referring to 10 cascading streams.\"\n  },\n\n  // ==========================================\n  // UNDERRATED DESTINATIONS (DISCOVERY GEMS)\n  // ==========================================\n  {\n    id: \"netarhat\",\n    name: \"Netarhat\",\n    tagline: \"The ethereal 'Queen of Chotanagpur' lost in pine mist\",\n    type: \"underrated\",\n    category: \"Hill Station & Pine Forests\",\n    district: \"Latehar\",\n    location: \"Western Plateau, 154 km from Ranchi\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.4833,\n      lng: 84.2667\n    },\n    elevation: \"1,128 m (3,700 ft)\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"Year-Round (Best Oct - March for clear sunrises)\",\n    timings: \"Open 24 Hours\",\n    entryFee: \"Free\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506744038136-46273834b3fb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506744038136-46273834b3fb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506744038136-46273834b3fb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1511497584788-87676104235f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1470071459604-3b5ec3a7fe05?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Perched atop an expansive flat laterite plateau at 1,128 meters, Netarhat is Jharkhand's most poetic secret. Known for its cool alpine breezes, towering British pine plantations, and the legendary Magnolia Sunset Point named after an English maiden's immortalized folklore, Netarhat offers unhurried tranquility away from modern urban rush.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Magnolia Point: Unmatched sunset over the Koel River valley\",\n      \"British-era pine forest trails smelling of fresh resin and mountain dew\",\n      \"Upper & Lower Ghaghri waterfalls nestled inside dense Sal groves\",\n      \"Cool hill climate with winter temperatures occasionally touching 1°C\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Ranchi Birsa Munda Airport (154 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Lohardaga Railway Station (85 km) or Ranchi (154 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Mesmerizing hill drive from Ranchi through Lohardaga with hairpin forested turns\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Carry warm woollens between November and February as temperatures drop sharply after sunset.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Avoid driving through isolated forest ghat sections late at night; plan your mountain transit during daylight hours.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"The British named it 'Nature's Hat' due to its bowl-shaped topography, which gradually evolved into the local name Netarhat.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"lodh-falls\",\n    name: \"Lodh Falls (Burha Ghaag)\",\n    tagline: \"Jharkhand's highest waterfall (143m) hidden in deep jungle\",\n    type: \"underrated\",\n    category: \"Wilderness & Waterfalls\",\n    district: \"Latehar\",\n    location: \"Near Mahuadanr, 195 km from Ranchi\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.5500,\n      lng: 84.0500\n    },\n    elevation: \"450 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"September to February\",\n    timings: \"08:00 AM - 04:30 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"₹10 per person\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1432405972618-c60b0225b8f9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1432405972618-c60b0225b8f9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1432405972618-c60b0225b8f9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1546548970-71785318a17b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Tumbling from a staggering height of 143 meters (469 feet) across multiple stepped tiers on the Burha River, Lodh Falls is the 21st highest waterfall in India and the undisputable champion of Jharkhand. Enveloped by pristine dense forests of the Palamu Tiger Reserve fringe, its roar can be heard from over 10 kilometres away.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Highest waterfall in Jharkhand with a 143-meter thunderous plunge\",\n      \"Multi-tiered natural amphitheater surrounded by ancient jungle\",\n      \"Pristine ecotourism sanctuary with raw, untouched wilderness\",\n      \"Ideal birdwatching habitat with hornbills, flycatchers & eagles\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Ranchi Airport (195 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Daltonganj Railway Station (120 km) or Latehar (90 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Accessible via Mahuadanr valley road from Netarhat (60 km) or Daltonganj\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Fuel up your vehicle completely before leaving Mahuadanr or Netarhat; no fuel pumps exist on the interior forest track.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Do not attempt to cross the river rapids or venture onto upper waterfall tiers; water levels surge rapidly without warning.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"The acoustic rumble of Lodh Falls is so intense during peak flow that locals call it 'The Thunder of Chotanagpur'.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"mccluskieganj\",\n    name: \"McCluskieganj\",\n    tagline: \"The nostalgic Anglo-Indian colonial sanctuary in the hills\",\n    type: \"underrated\",\n    category: \"Heritage & Living Culture\",\n    district: \"Ranchi\",\n    location: \"Northwest of Ranchi, 60 km away\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.6644,\n      lng: 85.0064\n    },\n    elevation: \"470 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"October to March\",\n    timings: \"Open 24 Hours\",\n    entryFee: \"Free (Homestays vary)\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513694203232-719a280e022f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513694203232-719a280e022f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513694203232-719a280e022f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1469854523086-cc02fe5d8800?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Founded in the 1930s by Ernest Timothy McCluskie as a dedicated homeland for the Anglo-Indian community, this quiet settlement is famous for its 300+ vintage European-style brick cottages, bakeries, orchards, and sleepy railway station immortalized in award-winning cinema (A Death in the Gunj).\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Heritage British-era colonial bungalows with gabled roofs and fireplaces\",\n      \"Dugadugi River bridge and quiet eucalyptus-lined cycle tracks\",\n      \"Unique heritage homestays serving Anglo-Indian culinary delicacies\",\n      \"Historic churches, convents, and serene peaceful cemetery gardens\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Birsa Munda Airport Ranchi (65 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"McCluskieganj Railway Station (MGME) right in the town\",\n      byRoad: \"Smooth 1.5-hour drive from Ranchi via Chanho and Khelari\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Book heritage homestays well in advance as room count is limited to preserve authentic local lifestyle.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Respect local residential privacy when photographing vintage private cottages and bungalow gardens.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"In the 1940s, more than 350 Anglo-Indian families lived here, creating an English countryside enclave with piano soirees in the heart of tribal forests.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"kiriburu-meghahatuburu\",\n    name: \"Kiriburu & Meghahatuburu\",\n    tagline: \"The legendary 'City of 700 Hills' inside the Saranda Forest\",\n    type: \"underrated\",\n    category: \"Endless Horizons & Forests\",\n    district: \"West Singhbhum\",\n    location: \"Border of Jharkhand & Odisha, 220 km from Ranchi\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 22.0833,\n      lng: 85.3500\n    },\n    elevation: \"900 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"November to March\",\n    timings: \"Open 24 Hours\",\n    entryFee: \"Free\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1511497584788-87676104235f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1511497584788-87676104235f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1511497584788-87676104235f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1470071459604-3b5ec3a7fe05?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Twin hill towns cradled within Saranda Forest — Asia's largest and most contiguous Sal forest covering over 800 square kilometers. Kiriburu ('Hill of Elephants') and Meghahatuburu ('Hill of Clouds') offer endless views over undulating forested ridges where the sun melts into an ocean of green canopy.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Meghahatuburu Sunset Point: Iconic views over 700 unbroken forested hills\",\n      \"Saranda forest: Asia's densest primeval Sal ecosystem\",\n      \"Purna Pani and Joro Waterfalls tucked inside untouched valleys\",\n      \"Vibrant Ho tribal folklore and indigenous heritage\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Ranchi (220 km) or Rourkela Airport (85 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Barbil Railway Station (25 km) or Manoharpur (45 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Best approached via Chaibasa or Rourkela on good state highways\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Ensure you obtain necessary forest transit passes from the West Singhbhum Forest Division if entering deep reserve zones.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Avoid solitary forest trails in deep Saranda; wild elephant herds actively migrate through this inter-state corridor.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"Saranda literally translates to 'The land of seven hundred hills' in the indigenous tribal tongue.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"dalma-wildlife-sanctuary\",\n    name: \"Dalma Wildlife Sanctuary\",\n    tagline: \"Hilltop sanctuary overlooking Jamshedpur & Subarnarekha\",\n    type: \"underrated\",\n    category: \"Wildlife & Hilltop Vista\",\n    district: \"East Singhbhum\",\n    location: \"Dalma Hills, 10 km from Jamshedpur\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 22.9000,\n      lng: 86.2167\n    },\n    elevation: \"926 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"October to April\",\n    timings: \"07:00 AM - 05:00 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"₹50 per person + Vehicle pass\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506744038136-46273834b3fb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Spread over 195 sq km across the Dalma mountain range towering 926 meters high, this sanctuary is famous for its resident Asian elephant population, barking deer, leopards, and ancient hilltop Shiva temple. The viewpoint at the summit provides breathtaking vistas of the industrial metropolis of Jamshedpur glowing beside the silver Subarnarekha River.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Dalma Summit Viewpoint with panoramic 360-degree plains views\",\n      \"Natural elephant habitat and canopy bird observation towers\",\n      \"Hilltop Shiva temple visited by forest pilgrims for generations\",\n      \"Pindrabera Forest Rest House perched right above the jungle valley\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Ranchi Birsa Munda Airport (125 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Tatanagar Junction Jamshedpur (18 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Smoothly accessible from NH-33 just 10 km north of Jamshedpur city\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Carry binoculars and drive under 20 km/h inside sanctuary limits to avoid startling wildlife.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Entry is closed after 5:00 PM; strictly adhere to ranger instructions regarding elephant herd movements.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"During the annual Sendra festival, tribal trackers traverse these hills in a tradition that predates modern recorded history.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"tagore-hill\",\n    name: \"Tagore Hill (Morabadi)\",\n    tagline: \"The serene philosopher's hill of the Tagore family in Ranchi\",\n    type: \"underrated\",\n    category: \"Culture & Philosophy\",\n    district: \"Ranchi\",\n    location: \"Morabadi, Ranchi City\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.4022,\n      lng: 85.3356\n    },\n    elevation: \"650 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"October to March (Mesmerizing at Sunrise/Sunset)\",\n    timings: \"06:00 AM - 06:30 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"₹10 per person\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513694203232-719a280e022f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513694203232-719a280e022f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513694203232-719a280e022f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506744038136-46273834b3fb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Rising 300 feet above the Ranchi plateau in Morabadi, Tagore Hill was the cherished sanctuary of Jyotirindranath Tagore (elder brother of Nobel Laureate Rabindranath Tagore). Here, atop the granite knoll, he built 'Shanti Dham' in 1908 and translated celebrated philosophical classics and composed plays in total contemplation.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Shanti Dham: Historic stone pavilion perched at the rocky peak\",\n      \"Brahmo Mandir and Tagore Art & Cultural exhibition museum\",\n      \"Sweeping panoramic vistas over Ranchi city and Morabadi grounds\",\n      \"Peaceful shaded stone pathways perfect for contemplative walks\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Birsa Munda Airport Ranchi (12 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Ranchi Railway Station (7 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Centrally situated in Morabadi, easily accessible by auto-rickshaw or taxi\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Take care when stepping on open granite surfaces during wet monsoon showers.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Do not climb beyond the designated boundary walls or railings on the cliff overlook.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"Rabindranath Tagore visited his brother here and drew deep inspiration from the Chotanagpur forest landscape for parts of 'Gitanjali'.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"itkhori-heritage\",\n    name: \"Itkhori Heritage Complex\",\n    tagline: \"Sacred confluence of Hindu, Buddhist & Jain antiquities\",\n    type: \"underrated\",\n    category: \"Archaeology & Heritage\",\n    district: \"Chatra\",\n    location: \"Mohane & Mahane River bank, Chatra District\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 24.2961,\n      lng: 85.1611\n    },\n    elevation: \"320 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"November to March (Itkhori Mahotsav in Feb)\",\n    timings: \"06:00 AM - 07:00 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"Free\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1582510003544-4d00b7f74220?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1582510003544-4d00b7f74220?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1582510003544-4d00b7f74220?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544735716-392fe2489ffa?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Nestled along the confluence of the Mohane and Mahane rivers, Itkhori is a remarkable archaeological treasure. Centered around the ancient Maa Bhadrakali Temple, excavations have revealed 9th-century Pala Dynasty Buddhist stupas with 1008 miniature Buddhas, Jain Tirthankara idols (Shitalnath), and intricate stone sculptures representing rare inter-faith harmony.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Ancient 9th-century Maa Bhadrakali black stone deity\",\n      \"Unique monolithic stupa carved with 1,008 miniature Buddha figures\",\n      \"Birthplace shrine of 10th Jain Tirthankara Bhagwan Shitalnath\",\n      \"Archaeological museum displaying Pala-era stone sculptures\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Gaya International Airport (75 km) or Ranchi Airport (140 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Koderma Junction (50 km) or Hazaribagh Road (70 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Smooth road connection off the GT Road (NH-19) via Chauparan (25 km)\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Hire an authorized archaeological trust guide to fully appreciate the complex iconography.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Touching, leaning on, or defacing exposed ancient stone relics and stupas is strictly punishable.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"Legend says Gautam Buddha's aunt arrived here searching for him; unable to convince him, she cried 'Iti Khoyi' ('I lost him here'), giving the town its name.\"\n  }\n];\n\n// Curated Informational Micro-Moments (\"Did You Know?\" editorial facts)\nconst DID_YOU_KNOW_FACTS = [\n  {\n    number: \"01\",\n    tag: \"ETYMOLOGY & NATURE\",\n    headline: \"Jharkhand literally means 'The Territory of Forests'\",\n    body: \"Derived from 'Jhar' (dense forest/bushland) and 'Khand' (land), over 29% of the state's geographical area is enveloped in primeval Sal, Mahua, and Teak woodland canopy.\"\n  },\n  {\n    number: \"02\",\n    tag: \"INDIGENOUS HERITAGE\",\n    headline: \"Home to 32 Unique Indigenous Tribal Communities\",\n    body: \"Rich in living ancestral wisdom, Jharkhand's Santhal, Munda, Oraon, Ho, and Birhor tribes maintain continuous thousand-year traditions in harmony with Mother Nature (Marang Buru).\"\n  },\n  {\n    number: \"03\",\n    tag: \"LIVING ART FORMS\",\n    headline: \"GI-Tagged Sohrai & Khovar Murals Painted with Natural Earth\",\n    body: \"Tribal women paint intricate ritual wall art using naturally sourced manganese black, ochre yellow, and white kaolin clay, a tradition dating back to prehistoric rock art.\"\n  },\n  {\n    number: \"04\",\n    tag: \"GEOLOGICAL WONDERS\",\n    headline: \"The Chotanagpur Plateau is over 2.5 Billion Years Old\",\n    body: \"Part of the ancient Gondwanaland supercontinent, this dramatic plateau features stepped knickpoints creating dozens of pristine waterfalls cascading across ancient granite.\"\n  }\n];\n\n// Travel Themes for Experience Showcase\nconst TRAVEL_THEMES = [\n  {\n    id: \"waterfalls\",\n    title: \"Roaring Waterfalls & Canyons\",\n    subtitle: \"From 143-meter thunderous plunges to serene emerald pools\",\n    count: \"15+ Cascades\",\n    image: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1546548970-71785318a17b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"wilderness\",\n    title: \"Untamed Wildlife & Sal Forests\",\n    subtitle: \"Asia's densest Sal reserves, wild elephant herds and tigers\",\n    count: \"4 Sanctuaries\",\n    image: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"spiritual\",\n    title: \"Sacred Summits & Ancient Shrines\",\n    subtitle: \"Revered Jyotirlingas, Jain mountain peaks, and timeless pilgrimages\",\n    count: \"8 Holy Sites\",\n    image: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1582510003544-4d00b7f74220?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"culture\",\n    title: \"Tribal Arts, Music & Living Traditions\",\n    subtitle: \"Sohrai murals, Dokra metalcraft, and vibrant seasonal harvest rhythms\",\n    count: \"32 Cultures\",\n    image: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513694203232-719a280e022f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80\"\n  }\n];\n","Description":"Write data.js with rich destination dataset, safety protocols, and coordinates","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\Bhavish Sawant\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\jharkhand-tourism\\js\\data.js","toolAction":"Writing data.js","toolSummary":"Writing data.js"}}]}
